      "description": "Watch Real Madrid vs Alcorcon highlights and goals from Friendly on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 24, 2026. In a high-energy preseason encounter, Real Madrid and Athletic Club faced off in a match that provided plenty of attacking flair and tactical intrigue. The contest, held on July 24, 2026 , saw both managers utilize their squads extensively in a clash defined by clinical finishing. Early Pressure and Breakthrough Real Madrid established their dominance early, controlling 74% of the possession throughout the match. The deadlock was broken in the 12th minute when Gonzalo Garcia found the back of the net with a precise right-footed strike, set up by a clever ball from Daniel Carvajal . The opening stages were not without tension, as Thiago Pitarch and Jude Bellingham both found themselves in the referee's book following early challenges. As the first half drew to a close, the game burst into life. In the 41st minute, Jude Bellingham doubled the lead for the hosts with a stunning left-footed volley after receiving a cross from Thiago Pitarch . However, Athletic Club responded almost immediately. In stoppage time, Inaki Williams turned provider for Gorka Guruzeta , who clinicaly volleyed home to reduce the deficit just before the halftime whistle. Second Half Dominance and VAR Drama The second half saw the introduction of fresh legs and a continued offensive push from Real Madrid . In the 51st minute, Kylian Mbappé extended the lead with a powerful effort from outside the box, assisted by Alvaro Carreras . Despite having several goals ruled out for offside, the French forward remained a constant threat to the Athletic Club backline. The drama intensified in the closing minutes. At the 88th minute, Brahim Díaz scored following a VAR review that overturned an initial decision, with Thiago Pitarch claiming another assist. Although Athletic Club managed a late consolation through an Urko Izeta header in the 91st minute—once again assisted by Inaki Williams — Real Madrid held firm to secure a 4-2 victory in an entertaining summer showcase."
